THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS INCLUDED IN THIS DATASET

The dataset is derived from and includes references to third-party data
provided under their own licenses. Users must comply with the terms of
these licenses when using the corresponding parts of the dataset.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Sentinel-1 GRD IW imagery (Copernicus Programme)

The Sentinel-1 SAR data used to produce the composites and water masks
are provided by the European Space Agency (ESA) under the free, full
and open Copernicus data policy, as defined in the Legal Notice on the
use of Copernicus Sentinel Data and Service Information:

  https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/documents/247904/690755/Sentinel_Data_Legal_Notice

Required attribution when using or redistributing this dataset
(including our processed derivatives) - as specified by the EU legal
notice:

  "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2024-2026, processed
   by Kzadri M., Begdouri A., El Fazazy K., Qjidaa H., Ouazzani Jamil M.,
   Tairi H., and Riffi J."

Users must also cite the dataset itself (see Suggested attribution
above) and, when applicable, the associated Data in Brief article.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

2. JRC Global Surface Water occurrence layer (auxiliary reference)

The auxiliary Global Surface Water occurrence layer included in this
dataset for contextual reference is derived from the JRC Global
Surface Water dataset, provided by the European Commission Joint
Research Centre (JRC) under an open license.

  Copyright (c) European Union, 1984-2021.

  Original reference:
    Pekel, J.-F., Cottam, A., Gorelick, N., & Belward, A. S. (2016).
    High-resolution mapping of global surface water and its long-term
    changes. Nature 540, 418-422.
    https://doi.org/10.1038/nature20584

  Dataset access:
    https://global-surface-water.appspot.com

This layer was included as contextual information only and was not
used to create or validate the Sentinel-1 water masks.

